# Applies ONLY to the StudioDO image: it is the one container entry whose
# `image_build_context` is this directory (see wrangler.jsonc). The AgentDO and
# DeployDO images still build with ./container as their context, which has no
# .dockerignore of its own, so nothing here affects them.
#
# That image COPYs exactly one file (container/studio-bringup.sh). Everything
# below is therefore dead weight in the context transfer — node_modules alone
# is ~605MB, which would otherwise be uploaded to the builder on every build.
node_modules
.wrangler
.git
page/dist

# Secrets. Not a size concern — a correctness one. This directory is now a
# docker build context, so anything left here is uploaded to the builder and
# can be baked into an image layer by a stray COPY. Three real ways a secret
# ends up here: test-integration/attach.e2e.ts WRITES .dev.vars into this
# directory before wrangler builds the studio image; the operator runs
# `wrangler deploy` from here per the finish list, with whatever .dev.vars or
# .env they keep locally; and a GitHub App PEM is the natural thing to drop
# next to wrangler.jsonc while setting GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.env
.env.*
*.pem
